A||N||2||capt_ron||A/C Question||||5||
Z||000000||capt_ron||05-14-2000||09:39 PM||||My girl friend drives my 87 SE to work everyday and tells me that the A/C isn't working. I checked the pressures and they are at 90PSI. The radiator fan comes on when the A/C is turned on but the compressor does not. I jumpered the pressure switch on the dryer but didn't get any results. I think that the compressor relay isn't energizing but I don't know where it is. There is not power at the compressor plug. Any ideas?<BR>Capt Ron||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiero Jon||05-14-2000||10:07 PM||||If your pressures are equal, your compressor isn't doing a thing.  Now it could be a number of things.  <BR>-The compressor clutch is bad or not getting power<P>-Any of the relays or switches could be out<BR>               -Pressure switches<BR>               -A/C Power relay (if vent fan works this isn't inop.<BR>               -A/C compressor control relay<BR>                (careful with that one it's tied to the ECM)<BR>               -A/C Cut-out switch (don't check this unless all else fails, it's only on V6s and it opens at extemely [425 psi] pressure. <BR>               -Compressor failure, if the pistons are shot the compressor won't work at all.<P>To do the electical test, I'd do the following<P>Turn on the A/C and if the clutch clicks into place all the relays are working.<P>If not e-mail me and I can walk you through the checks.<P>Jon<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||capt_ron||05-14-2000||10:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero Jon:<BR><B>If your pressures are equal, your compressor isn't doing a thing.  Now it could be a number of things.  <BR>-The compressor clutch is bad or not getting power<P>-Any of the relays or switches could be out<BR>               -Pressure switches<BR>               -A/C Power relay (if vent fan works this isn't inop.<BR>               -A/C compressor control relay<BR>                (careful with that one it's tied to the ECM)<BR>               -A/C Cut-out switch (don't check this unless all else fails, it's only on V6s and it opens at extemely [425 psi] pressure. <BR>               -Compressor failure, if the pistons are shot the compressor won't work at all.<P>To do the electical test, I'd do the following<P>Turn on the A/C and if the clutch clicks into place all the relays are working.<P>If not e-mail me and I can walk you through the checks.<P>Jon<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The compressor clutch is not getting power to energize. The pressures are with the egine off. BTW I have a certification so I know all the checks but I can't track down the relays.<BR>||||reg||1
